    rcap:evidencePosition "lead_in:3" ;
    rcap:evidenceSection "8.3.4" ;
    rcap:evidenceText "In adults and in children 9 years of age and older, baricitinib will be administered enterally at a dose of 4 mg daily if the eGFR is at least 60 mL/min/1.73m 2 ." ;
    rcap:occurrenceKind "intervention" .

[] a owl:Axiom ;
    owl:annotatedProperty rdfs:subClassOf ;
    owl:annotatedSource rcap:DomainDesign_IIM ;
    owl:annotatedTarget _:N486a84acfdf84f1fa768bbbbb644911f ;
    rcap:evidenceDoc "Influenza Immune Modulation Domain-Specific Appendix 2.1" ;
    rcap:evidenceGlyph "•" ;
    rcap:evidencePage 27 ;
    rcap:evidencePosition "3" ;
    rcap:evidenceSection "8.2.3" ;
    rcap:evidenceText "It is recognised that there is a wide range of regulatory approaches and attitudes to the evaluation of interventions in pregnant trial participants across participating regions and sites. Known or suspected pregnancy is not an intervention-level exclusion for the tocilizumab intervention by default; however, if a site does not have regulatory approval to enrol pregnant patients to the tocilizumab intervention, known or suspected pregnancy will be applied as an intervention-specific exclusion and will result in exclusion from the tocilizumab intervention." ;
    rcap:occurrenceKind "intervention_exclusion" .

